[Music]  the world  in which each of us and all of us now  live  is full of pressing problems and future  risks  but it is also full of hope aspiration  and opportunity  public leaders can come in many  different guises they can be ordinary  citizens who take up a local cause  they can manage a non-profit  organization or a voluntary association  that provides services to those in need  and security to those who are oppressed  they can be individuals who run for  elective office  hoping to create more economic social or  political equality  they can serve in government hoping to  increase the responsiveness  efficiency effectiveness and fairness of  government operations  in leadership creating public value you  will learn how to face and meet the  challenge  of diagnosing the reality you confront  and designing a public value proposition  that is both  plausibly value creating and actionable  by you and your particular context  through case studies you will see real  public leaders seeking to challenge the  status quo  you'll be asked to reflect on their  thought and action using the analytic  frameworks and concepts developed and  applied throughout the course  the goal is simple learn how to create  long-term public value by envisioning  and enacting a better more just future  for us all  [Music]

